# Loaded by `vite build --mode test`, and by nothing else.
#
# It exists so the appearance suite (playwright.visual.config.ts) can diff a
# REAL production build while its requests still land on the stub worker the
# e2e fixtures route. Without it the build would take `.env.production` and
# call `https://api.agentsinc.sh` — an origin no stub claims, and one the
# fixture's third-party guard does not watch either, so the captures would
# quietly be of whatever the live API happened to return.
#
# Committed like `.env.production` and for the same reason: it is not a
# secret, it is the one place this address is written down, and a copy of it
# somewhere else is a way for the two to disagree. Do not add a secret here.

VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
